\begin_layout Standard
The least significant bit gives the sign and the other three bits give the emoji index,
 so the sixteen possible outcomes are the eight emojis in two signs.
 Two cards match when they show the same emoji with opposite signs,
 which gives eight pairs on the board.
 The method 
\family typewriter
generate_deck
\family default
 (line 150 of the same file) runs the four-qubit circuit with one measurement per run,
 keeps only the cards not yet obtained,
 and stops when all sixteen are collected.
 The order on the board is then shuffled classically with random.shuffle.
\end_layout

