\begin_layout Standard
Mapping of the observables on hardware.
 On a real processor the transpiler places the two qubits of the experiment on physical qubits of its choice,
 in a device that has more than one hundred qubits.
 For this reason each observable is remapped with the layout produced by the transpiler (Listing 3).
 Without this step the expectation values would refer to different qubits from those of the circuit,
 and the Bloch vectors would be meaningless.
 All six single-qubit observables are sent in a single job,
 which also limits the use of the available quantum time.
\end_layout

